meta {
  name: 33 Update Note Print Sections
  type: http
  seq: 33
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/note-print-sections
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "excludedSections": ["limitations", "references"]
  }
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("returns the report's notes-print state", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    expect(d).to.have.property("enabled");
    expect(d).to.have.property("isPanelMember");
    expect(d.excludedSections).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

docs {
  Choose which of the five Notes sections are LEFT OUT of this report's
  printed version (the checkbox beside each section on the report: checked
  prints, unchecked is left out).

  Body: `excludedSections` - the FULL list of section keys to leave out; it
  replaces the stored list. Allowed keys: `useful_for`, `interpretation`,
  `limitations`, `remarks`, `references` (anything else is a 400; duplicates
  are a 400). An empty list means all five print. The list is stored on this report
  only (`lab_reports.excluded_note_sections`), and the first save marks the report as
  having a choice of its own (`lab_reports.has_chosen_note_print`); until then the Branch
  Setting decides the default. Approval writes the default down, so an approved report
  prints the same forever, even if the Branch Setting changes later. Re-run and Repeat
  reset the report to no choice yet.

  Allowed only while the report is Pending, Partial Pending or Saved (409
  `LAB_REPORT_PARAMETER_NOTE_NOT_EDITABLE` otherwise).

  It only changes the PRINTED and SHARED PDF (single print, Print All, Share
  Email / WhatsApp attachment). It never changes what the screen shows.

  It works whether the matching Branch Setting (Branch Admin > Branch Settings > Technician
  Settings > Report Printing) is ON or OFF: that setting only sets the default selection (the
  **Lab Panel** switch `isLabPanelNotesSelectable` for a report whose order line is a panel,
  the **Lab Test** switch `isLabTestNotesSelectable` for a single test, read from the branch
  that HOLDS the report). A free-text line has no Notes: nothing is saved and the current
  state (`enabled: false`) comes back unchanged.

  Response: `{ enabled, isPanelMember, excludedSections }`. The same object is
  returned as `notesPrint` by `GET /lab-reports/:id`.

  No permission key by design. The report's write locks still apply: 409
  `LAB_REPORT_LOCKED` if locked; a sent-out, cancelled-order or removed-test
  report is refused; 404 `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND` if missing/other-tenant/other-branch.
  The choice is cleared when the report is returned for a repeat, and kept on
  Re-Run.
}
